-------
For research centers: 

Please note that our license is usually a "group license", i.e. it allows (unlimited) use of Quanty within a research group.

But this also means, that a license for a computing center does NOT allow all users of this center to use the Quanty code. Instead, every user should have it's own (private) license and only then he would be allowed to use Quanty also on your hardware.

We would request that you INFORM your users about this regulation, but we do not insist that you enforce (or check) this regulation, so that no extra effort is necessary from your side (besides giving the info mentioned above) to your users.

However, we do request that you make sure that users cannot copy the source code illegally.

Note that this currently means users (one per group) should register at www.quanty.org. This helps me to create an overview of active users of the code.

We furthermore request that the version of the code available to the community at your research center is in agrement with the actual version on www.quanty.org